# Deploy AudioPlayer app after code changes

Only the release build may be installed on the phone. The `.debug` variant must never be left on the
device: it shows up as a second app, holds its own media session and notification, and competes for
the media button with the real app.

When you finish changes under the Android Gradle project at `c:\Users\Volkr\Desktop\audioPlayer`:

1. From PowerShell: `Set-Location "c:\Users\Volkr\Desktop\audioPlayer"; .\gradlew.bat installRelease`
2. Confirm the build reports `Installed on 1 device` (or fix adb/device issues if install fails).

Do this automatically at the end of the task whenever the Android app sources were modified, unless
the user explicitly asks not to install.

## Debug builds

Never run `installDebug`. Debug logging (Timber output) is only available in the debug variant, so if
a problem cannot be diagnosed from the release build:

1. Install it temporarily: `.\gradlew.bat installDebug`
2. Collect the logs.
3. Uninstall it again in the same task: `adb uninstall com.generic.audioplayes.debug`

A snapshot of the debug variant's data taken before it was removed lives in `debug-backup/`
(untracked, contains personal library data) — see the README there for how to restore it.
